  "name": "claudeconnect",
  "version": "2.15.0",
  "released": "2026-10-19",
  "notes": [
    "Updates now install by themselves. One starts only while no reply is being written, waits again before replacing the site and before restarting the program on your computer, and a message sent during that restart waits for the new program, so nothing is cut short.",
    "Nothing on the page changes while it happens: messages aren't paused and the page doesn't reload. The top bar says Update coming, then Updated · Reload, and you reload whenever you like.",
    "An update that needs something from you (a permission on your computer, a password, an answer) doesn't install by itself: Settings → Updates says why, with Update now.",
    "Update automatically can be turned off in Settings → Updates. This one version still needs Update now once: the ones after it install by themselves."
  ],
